.8912,13.6809],[100.768,13.7766],[100.095,13.6892],[99.8467,13.5057],[99.947,13.3876],[99.9006,12.9889],[99.7768,12.7307],[99.7939,12.3155],[99.5417,12.0693],[99.5018,11.7752],[99.3616,11.5991],[99.0984,10.8317],[98.8436,10.5438],[98.7789,9.8524],[98.8839,9.464],[99.0058,9.3474],[99.3544,9.4127],[99.4232,9.4798],[99.5491,9.426],[99.5774,8.845],[99.6522,8.6627],[99.8161,8.5281],[99.9145,8.0352],[99.9041,7.8679],[99.7246,7.7516],[99.7613,7.65],[100.2084,7.2225],[100.9181,7.2083],[101.1724,7.1423],[101.1581,6.9123],[101.008,6.923],[100.8907,6.7692]]],"note":{"en":"A fixed reference from one 1580 illustration, shown during 1569–1580 for comparison with Ayutthaya’s subordinate-court period. It is not an annual boundary or an outline of direct military occupation. The author warns that borders were not demarcated; one color combines different dependencies. Scholarly analysis distinguishes tributary Ayutthaya and Lan Xang from more direct rule near Pegu. The source is cropped to the south, so that edge is intentionally open. Alignment to fourteen modern city references has median residual about 26 km and maximum about 80 km; historical uncertainty is greater.","zh":"以一幅1580年示意图的固定范围，在1569—1580年间供比较阿瑜陀耶的附属宫廷时期。这不是逐年边界，也不是直接军事占领区轮廓。作者提醒当时并无划定的边界；同一种颜色合并了不同依附关系。学术研究区分阿瑜陀耶、澜沧的朝贡地位与勃固附近较直接的统治。原图南侧被裁切，因此此处故意留开。与14个现代城市参照点对齐的残差中位数约26公里，最大约80公里；历史不确定性更大。"},"sources":[{"title":"Map of Taungoo Empire (1580)","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Taungoo_Empire_(1580).png","publisher":"Soewinhan / Wikimedia Commons","checkedAt":"2026-10-27","evidenceNote":"Inspected source image and warning about undemarcated, approximate borders; green area combines dependencies and the image is cropped in the south. Source bibliography was not independently verified for the outline."},{"title":"Thai-Burmese Warfare During the Sixteenth Century and the Growth of the First Toungoo Empire","url":"https://thesiamsociety.org/wp-content/uploads/2005/03/JSS_093_0c_PamareeSurakiat_ThaiBurmeseWarfareDuring16thCentu.pdf","publisher":"Pamaree Surakiat / Journal of the Siam Society","checkedAt":"2026-10-27","evidenceNote":"Inspected pp.91–92 and 95–97. Treats Ayutthaya and Lan Xang as tributaries, alongside more direct control near Pegu; does not validate the traced sphere perimeter."}],"contextValidity":{"start":1569,"end":1580,"backwardReviewed":true,"reviewedAt":"2026-10-27","evidence":["https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Taungoo_Empire_(1580).png","https://thesiamsociety.org/wp-content/uploads/2005/03/JSS_093_0c_PamareeSurakiat_ThaiBurmeseWarfareDuring16thCentu.pdf"],"note":{"en":"A fixed reference from one 1580 illustration, shown during 1569–1580 for comparison with Ayutthaya’s subordinate-court period. It is not an annual boundary or an outline of direct military occupation. The author warns that borders were not demarcated; one color combines different dependencies. Scholarly analysis distinguishes tributary Ayutthaya and Lan Xang from more direct rule near Pegu. The source is cropped to the south, so that edge is intentionally open. Alignment to fourteen modern city references has median residual about 26 km and maximum about 80 km; historical uncertainty is greater.","zh":"以一幅1580年示意图的固定范围，在1569—1580年间供比较阿瑜陀耶的附属宫廷时期。这不是逐年边界，也不是直接军事占领区轮廓。作者提醒当时并无划定的边界；同一种颜色合并了不同依附关系。学术研究区分阿瑜陀耶、澜沧的朝贡地位与勃固附近较直接的统治。原图南侧被裁切，因此此处故意留开。与14个现代城市参照点对齐的残差中位数约26公里，最大约80公里；历史不确定性更大。"}},"pixelTrace":{"maskedPixels":319030,"closingPixels":4,"cutoffRow":1113,"simplificationPixels":2,"affine":[[0.02162574381059904,0.0014712537748429236],[-0.001304235810811884,-0.020906780588866778],[90.72800534584067,29.2275231947552]],"controlPoints":14,"medianResidualKm":26,"maximumResidualKm":80}},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[98.2441,29.2392],[98.3483,29.1839],[98.459,29.233],[98.4984,29.1733],[98.7847,29.276],[98.7146,29.188],[98.7959,29.1102],[98.7547,28.7952],[99.2378,28.599],[99.2425,28.3287],[99.4076,28.215],[99.3782,28.0881],[99.4582,27.9895],[99.3664,27.9],